ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# One switch picks the whole data stack (see backend/config.py):
#   APP_MODE=real (default) → journal.db      + Keep sync on
#   APP_MODE=demo           → demo_journal.db + Keep sync off
# Leave DATABASE_URL / SYNC_ON_STARTUP unset so APP_MODE can derive them; set one
# only to override that single piece. Don't re-pin the real defaults here — that
# silently neutralises APP_MODE=demo.
# APP_MODE=real
#
# Postgres (ADR 0003 — the real DB going forward). Start the local server with
# `docker compose up -d db` (see docker-compose.yml), then point the app at it:
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://journal:journal@localhost:5432/journal
# Unset → APP_MODE derives SQLite (journal.db real / demo_journal.db demo), which
# is still what tests and the demo use. Vector search is Postgres-only.
# The schema is managed by Alembic (`alembic upgrade head`).
#
# Run that upgrade during app startup. On (default) keeps dev a one-liner. Set to
# 0 in production and run `alembic upgrade head` as an explicit deploy step —
# otherwise DDL hits real data with no human checkpoint and N workers race to
# apply it. A failed migration now aborts boot rather than serving on an unknown
# schema, so a misconfigured DATABASE_URL fails loudly instead of 500ing.
# AUTO_MIGRATE=0
#
# Skip the startup Keep sync during dev so `uvicorn --reload` doesn't re-sync
# on every save (real mode syncs by default):
# SYNC_ON_STARTUP=0

# Freemium daily LLM budgets in dollars, UTC-day window (ADR 0003, F2).
# The quota gate refuses an LLM call once spend >= budget — BEFORE spending.
# Defaults: free tier $0 (keyless users get a friendly refusal; BYO keys are
# F4), demo $1 (keeps the showcase alive), global cap $5 (the kill-switch —
# bounds the worst day the shared API key can have, system work included).
# FREE_TIER_DAILY_USD=0
# DEMO_DAILY_USD=1
# GLOBAL_DAILY_USD=5

# Public demo (hosting shape B): when on, an unauthenticated request falls back to
# the seeded demo user (read-only, DEMO_DAILY_USD budget) instead of 401 — so a
# visitor without an account lands in the demo, and signing in gives them their own
# journal in the SAME app. Off (default) = private instance (logged-out → 401).
# Seed the demo first: `DATABASE_URL=…pg…  python scripts/seed_demo.py`.
# PUBLIC_DEMO=1

# Google Keep ingestion (omit to disable Keep sync entirely):
GOOGLE_EMAIL=you@gmail.com
GOOGLE_APP_MASTER_TOKEN=aas_et/...

# Sign in with Google (multi-user auth — ADR 0003). NOT the Keep creds above.
# From Google Cloud Console → APIs & Services → Credentials → Create OAuth
# client ID → type "Web application", authorized redirect URI:
#   http://localhost:8000/auth/callback
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=....apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=GOCSPX-...
#
# Signs the short-lived cookie carrying the in-flight OAuth state. Unset →
# random per boot (fine in dev; a restart only drops logins mid-handshake).
# Pin in production: python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_hex(32))"
# SESSION_SECRET=
#
# Where /auth/callback sends the browser after login (the SPA origin):
# FRONTEND_URL=http://localhost:5173
#
# `Secure` on the session cookie. On by default. Browsers accept Secure cookies
# on http://localhost, so dev needs no change — set 0 only when serving dev over
# a plain-http LAN address. Never set 0 in production: it is what keeps the
# session token off the wire when someone is nudged to http://.
# COOKIE_SECURE=1

# Where fastembed caches the ~90 MB embedding model. Unset → the system temp
# dir, which cold starts wipe, turning the first search into a synchronous
# download inside the request. backend/Dockerfile bakes the model in at
# /opt/fastembed and sets this for you; set it by hand only outside Docker.
# FASTEMBED_CACHE_DIR=/opt/fastembed

# GoodNotes ingestion. Point at the local folder holding the exported PDF
# (e.g. the Google Drive Desktop mirror of the GoodNotes backup). Requires a
# terminal with Full Disk Access (System Settings → Privacy → Full Disk Access).
# Plain path, no shell escaping — dotenv takes the value literally.
GOODNOTES_PATH=~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-you@gmail.com/My Drive/GoodNotes/Notes
#
# Minutes between scheduled GoodNotes folder scans. 0 (default) = off; a
# positive value picks up newly-appended pages on a timer.
# GOODNOTES_SCAN_INTERVAL_MIN=60


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Production deploy manifest
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MUST be set (the app is wrong or insecure without them):
#   DATABASE_URL              managed Postgres, with the pgvector extension
#                             available. If the password contains reserved
#                             characters it must be URL-encoded (%40 for @).
#   ANTHROPIC_API_KEY         the operator key; every keyless user spends on it
#   APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY        Fernet key for BYO keys at rest. Losing or rotating
#                             it makes every stored user key undecryptable.
#   SESSION_SECRET            pin it, or multi-worker OAuth login breaks: the
#                             state cookie is signed per-process
#   FRONTEND_URL              the SPA origin — also the CORS allow-list entry
#   GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID    with the production redirect URI registered in the
#   GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET  Google console: https://<api-host>/auth/callback
#   AUTO_MIGRATE=0            run `alembic upgrade head` as a deploy step instead
#
# SHOULD be reviewed before going live:
#   COOKIE_SECURE=1           (default) — leave it on
#   GLOBAL_DAILY_USD          the kill-switch. This is the hard bound on what a
#                             bad day can cost you. Set it deliberately low.
#   PUBLIC_DEMO               leave UNSET unless you have read the caveat below
#
# LEAVE UNSET in production:
#   GOOGLE_EMAIL / GOOGLE_APP_MASTER_TOKEN / GOODNOTES_PATH — the connector sync
#   routes resolve their owner from GOOGLE_EMAIL and ignore the caller, so with
#   these set any signed-in user can trigger a sync into that account.
#
# PUBLIC_DEMO caveat: it makes every route reachable with no credential at all,
# resolving to the shared demo account. There is no rate limiting anywhere in the
# app, and the quota gate is read-then-act, so concurrent requests can overshoot
# DEMO_DAILY_USD before any of them records spend. GLOBAL_DAILY_USD is the only
# hard stop. Do not enable it without a per-IP rate limit in front.
